Gears of War 3: the black blotches on animated faces. A vertex buffer whose fetch constant kept the same
address and size was never requested again, even after the swap cleared its in-sync bit, so a buffer
the CPU rewrites in place each frame (the facial morph buffer) reached the face depth pre-pass with
the previous frame's data, while the base and lighting passes - after another buffer had used the
slot - got the current frame's. Where the face moved away from the camera both colour passes failed
their depth test against the pre-pass. Every out-of-sync vertex buffer is now requested, as in Xenia.
gpu_vertex_buffer_state_skip (default false) restores the old skip. Found by Gemini 4 Argon from the
investigation handoff.

--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
@@ -82,6 +82,10 @@
   }
 }
 }  // namespace
+
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(gpu_vertex_buffer_state_skip, false, "GPU",
+                    "Old behaviour: skip requesting a vertex buffer whose address and size match the last "
+                    "draw on that slot, even in a new frame (stale CPU-written data)");
 
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(d3d12_readback_memexport, false, "GPU/D3D12",
                     "Read data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU")
@@ -2840,7 +2844,15 @@
           return false;
       }
       VertexBufferState& state = vertex_buffer_states_[vfetch_index];
-      if (state.address == vfetch_constant.address && state.size == vfetch_constant.size) {
+      // The in-sync bit is cleared at every swap so each buffer is requested again in a new frame
+      // (the CPU may have rewritten it in place, like Gears of War 3's facial morph buffer). Skipping
+      // the request because the address and size are unchanged defeated that: the first draw of a
+      // frame then used the previous frame's data from shared memory, and later draws (after another
+      // buffer had been bound to the slot) the current frame's - the face depth pre-pass and colour
+      // passes disagreed and the colour passes failed their depth test (black blotches). Xenia
+      // requests every vertex buffer of every draw.
+      if (REXCVAR_GET(gpu_vertex_buffer_state_skip) && state.address == vfetch_constant.address &&
+          state.size == vfetch_constant.size) {
         vertex_buffers_in_sync_[vfetch_index >> 6] |= vfetch_bit;
         continue;
       }
